            "properties": {
                "0": {
                    "name": "block",
                    "value": "Finds the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a symmetric matrix: the directions it only stretches, without turning, and how much it stretches along each.\n\nIts most common use is principal component analysis. Feed it the covariance matrix of some data (np.cov) and the eigenvectors are the data's principal axes - the direction it varies most along, then the next most at right angles to that, and so on - and the eigenvalues say how much variance lies along each. The first axis of a cloud of hand positions is the main direction of the gesture; the first few axes of many joints are the main ways the body moves together.\n\nSYNTAX:\nnp.linalg.eigh\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\nmatrix:\nA square, symmetric matrix (equal to its own transpose), such as a covariance or correlation matrix. Only its lower triangle is read, so a matrix that is not symmetric gives the answer for a different matrix. Every input is analysed and sent.\n\norder:\nAn option, under the node: largest first (the default here, the principal axis first) or smallest first (the order NumPy itself gives).\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\neigenvalues:\nHow much the matrix stretches along each eigenvector.\n\neigenvectors:\nOne eigenvector per COLUMN, in the same order as the eigenvalues, each of length 1. Sent first. The sign of each is arbitrary: (0.71, 0.71) and (-0.71, -0.71) are the same axis.\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\nSix points lying close to the diagonal line y = x. Their covariance, analysed: the first eigenvalue (6.95) is hundreds of times the second (0.01), and the first eigenvector, the first column, is about (0.71, 0.71) - the diagonal, the direction the points run along. The second axis, at right angles, holds almost nothing: the points barely stray from the line. The round node only tidies the numbers.\n\nRELATED:\nnp.cov makes the covariance matrix to feed it. np.linalg.svd does the same job for any matrix, symmetric or not. t.linalg.eig is the PyTorch version;\nt.linalg.pca_low_rank does a whole PCA in one step.",
                    "value_type": "str"
                },
